Package: h340-usb-backup
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ehsan Enaloo <19691857+ehsanenaloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), mount, systemd
Recommends: acer-h340-usb-backup-dkms, h340-leds
Replaces: openmediavault-h340 (<< 0.5.0)
Breaks: openmediavault-h340 (<< 0.5.0)
Description: Acer H340 one-touch USB Backup copy service
 Waits for the front USB Backup button of an Acer Aspire easyStore H340 and
 copies the device on the front USB port to a folder you choose. The source is
 mounted read-only, nothing is deleted or overwritten, every file is verified
 after copying, and each run gets its own dated folder. Insertion of a device
 never starts a copy.
 Works on any systemd system. The button needs the kernel module from the
 acer-h340-usb-backup-dkms package. The service starts only when
 /etc/h340-usb-backup.json exists; an example is in
 /usr/share/doc/h340-usb-backup. The openmediavault-h340 plugin writes that
 file from its settings page.
